{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>מלשני</b> — The yod is added and it is an adjective; its meaning is like מלשין (informer)." "<b>אצמית</b> — Like royal decrees. Or: <b>אצמית רכילותו</b> — only one who is רחב לבב (broad of heart); and the meaning is very wise, like 'and one who is רחב לב I cannot אצמיתו,' for by his wisdom he guards his soul and his words. And some say: him I cannot look upon, or: I cannot be with him — and this is closer."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 101, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:42.062642441Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}